---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How It Works — Optical Typography Analysis Blueprint | Font Finder"
  description="Learn how Font Finder identifies typefaces from images using optical letterform geometry, stroke contrast, serifs, and aspect ratios. No AI hallucinations."
>
  <article class="py-12 sm:py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-[1000px] mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <div class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#e4f222]"></div>
        <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#8a8f98]">TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.022em]">
        How Font Finder Works
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] text-[#8a8f98] leading-relaxed font-normal">
        A technical deep dive into in-browser letterform extraction, geometric property calculation, and catalog distance matching.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[#8a8f98]">
      
      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-normal text-[#e4f222]">01</span>
          <h2 class="text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.011em]">
            Adaptive Contrast Binarization
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[#d0d6e0]">
          The canvas binarizer inspects edge luminance across image perimeters to evaluate background polarity (dark-on-light vs. light-on-dark). Using Rec. 709 luminance weighing (<code class="font-mono text-[12px] text-[#d0d6e0] bg-[#161718] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-[#23252a]">0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B</code>), pixels are dynamically separated into foreground letter ink and background.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-normal text-[#e4f222]">02</span>
          <h2 class="text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.011em]">
            Character Bounding & Line Projections
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[#d0d6e0]">
          Horizontal and vertical pixel histograms detect line baselines, cap heights, and character bounding envelopes. Artifacts, photo noise, and decorative borders are stripped out using aspect filters.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-normal text-[#e4f222]">03</span>
          <h2 class="text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.011em]">
            Typographic Metric Extraction
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 font-mono text-[12px]">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-[6px] bg-[#161718] border border-[#23252a]">
            <span class="text-[#ffffff] font-normal block mb-1">Terminal Serifs</span>
            <span class="text-[#8a8f98]">Detects horizontal feet and brackets at baseline to identify serif typefaces.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-[6px] bg-[#161718] border border-[#23252a]">
            <span class="text-[#ffffff] font-normal block mb-1">Aspect Geometry</span>
            <span class="text-[#8a8f98]">Separates condensed (&lt;0.50), regular (~0.62), and geometric wide (&gt;0.68).</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-[6px] bg-[#161718] border border-[#23252a]">
            <span class="text-[#ffffff] font-normal block mb-1">Stroke Contrast</span>
            <span class="text-[#8a8f98]">Ratio of vertical stem to horizontal hairline thickness.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-[6px] bg-[#161718] border border-[#23252a]">
            <span class="text-[#ffffff] font-normal block mb-1">Weight Density</span>
            <span class="text-[#8a8f98]">Translates stem thickness directly into standard CSS font weights (300–900).</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section class="rounded-[12px] border border-[#23252a] bg-[#0f1011] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-normal text-[#e4f222]">04</span>
          <h2 class="text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] font-[510] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.011em]">
            Verified Google Fonts Distance Scoring
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[#d0d6e0]">
          Calculated vectors are scored against pre-indexed Google Fonts metadata. The closest match is ranked with an exact confidence percentage and instant CSS blueprint generation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="pt-3">
        <a
          href="/#finder"
          class="btn-acid-lime"
        >
          <span>Launch Font Finder</span>
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 ml-2" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
